Kubernetes operates on a declarative reconciliation loop (desired state == current state). 
You can test both immediate crash recovery and probe-driven restarts.

1.Open a real-time cluster watcher:

Run in a separate terminal.

Keep this watch command active so you see pod status transitions, terminations, and restarts live:

kubectl get pods -n mini-project-1 -w

2.Test 1: Manual Pod Deletion (ReplicaSet Recovery):

Delete one of the running frontend pods:

TARGET_POD=$(kubectl get pods -n mini-project-1 -l app=frontend -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}')
kubectl delete pod $TARGET_POD -n mini-project-1

What happens under the hood:

The pod enters Terminating.

The Deployment controller detects current replicas (1) < desired replicas (2).

A replacement pod is immediately scheduled and initialized, keeping your application online without dropped traffic.

3.Test 2: Process Crash Simulation (SIGKILL):

Kill the main container process inside a running pod directly:

TARGET_POD=$(kubectl get pods -n mini-project-1 -l app=frontend -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}')
kubectl exec -n mini-project-1 $TARGET_POD -- kill 1

What happens under the hood:

The container process exits with a non-zero code.

The local node kubelet notices the container died and applies the pod’s restartPolicy: Always.

The pod’s RESTARTS count increments by 1, and the pod returns to Running in 1–2 seconds.

4.Test 3: Liveness Probe Failure Simulation:

Break the Redis liveness probe condition to watch the kubelet actively intervene:

# Kill the redis-server process directly inside the Redis container
REDIS_POD=$(kubectl get pods -n mini-project-1 -l app=redis -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}')
kubectl exec -n mini-project-1 $REDIS_POD -- redis-cli -a SuperSecureK8sPassword123! shutdown

What happens under the hood:

The TCP/exec probe fails consecutively past the failureThreshold.

The kubelet sends a SIGTERM followed by a SIGKILL to restart the container automatically.


